-- title:
--   Functions on the quotient Drinfeld curve regular at all affine places
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$, and assume the coordinate ring `CoordRing q κ` — the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1` — is a domain; write $F =$ `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` for its fraction field. Let $C$ be a subgroup of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$, and let $z \in F$. Assume first that $z$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ C`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32), the intermediate field of $F/\kappa$ fixed by the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` $\langle(1,\zeta)\rangle$ for $\zeta \in C$. Assume second that for every $v :$ [`AlgebraicCurve.Place κ F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22) — that is, every valuation subring of $F$ that contains the image of $\kappa$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring — such that the images of the elements `x q κ` and `y q κ` of the coordinate ring lie in the valuation subring of $v$, the element $z$ also lies in that valuation subring. Then there is $b$ in `CoordRing q κ` fixed by `muAction q κ ζ` for every $\zeta \in C$ and whose image in $F$ is $z$.
--
--   This is the statement that a function on the quotient of the affine Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ which is regular at every place where the two coordinates are regular is (the image of) a $C$-invariant element of the coordinate ring. It is used in the analysis of the supersingular part of the semistable covering of the modular curve at full level, in particular for the stalk computations at smooth points of the affine charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_exists_muAction_eq_and_algebraMap_eq_of_mem_quotField_of_forall_place.lean

